# Extra environment for start-chromium.sh. Installed to /etc/pioneer-tv/chromium.env.
# The board (Pi 3 or Pi 4/5) and the resolution come from board.env; only put
# overrides here.
#
# Extra Chromium flags:
# PIONEER_TV_CHROMIUM_FLAGS="--force-device-scale-factor=1"
#
# GPU flags. Default on a Pi 4/5: GPU compositing and rasterisation. Default on
# a Pi 3: --disable-gpu (its GPU cannot give Chromium a GLES 3 context). Set to
# an empty string to let Chromium decide on its own.
# PIONEER_TV_GPU_FLAGS="--disable-gpu"
#
# Video decoding: "software" (default on a Pi 4) or "hardware". The Pi's
# decoder wedges on every resolution change, which is what makes SVT Play
# pause; software decode costs about one core and never stalls.
# PIONEER_TV_VIDEO_DECODE=hardware
#
# PIONEER_TV_PROFILE=/home/pi/.pioneer-tv/chromium
